<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    The entry point for an MTP test run on browser-wasm when the test
    project cannot host one itself - which is to say, when it is F#.

    The wasm runtime awaits an `async Task<int> Main`, and only finds one
    by recognising the C# compiler's synchronous stub (IL `specialname`,
    a `<Main>` name) and looking past it. Microsoft.Testing.Platform.
    MSBuild's F# entry-point template has no such stub - F# has no async
    Main to wrap - so it ends in `Async.RunSynchronously`, which on the
    single-threaded wasm runtime blocks the only thread the first time
    MTP suspends. The banner prints, then nothing, forever. Found by
    porting a real F# suite.

    So the entry point lives here instead, in a C# assembly the test
    project merely references (this ships inside the AnyUnit.
    TestingPlatform package's lib folder), and the JS harness starts the
    runtime with `dotnet.withMainAssembly("AnyUnit.TestingPlatform.WasmEntry")`.
    Main does what the generated entry point would have: build the MTP
    app, register every TestingPlatformBuilderHook in reach, run. Which
    assembly holds the tests comes from the AnyUnit.TestAssembly runtime
    host configuration option the targets emit (AppContext data at run
    time), since this assembly is the entry assembly and carries no
    metadata of the test project's own.

    netstandard2.0 + OutputType Exe: an entry-point token is all the
    runtime needs, and netstandard keeps it loadable by any wasm TFM.
    UseAppHost=false because there is no desktop host for it, on purpose.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>netstandard2.0</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>9.0</LangVersion>
    <UseAppHost>false</UseAppHost>
    <IsTestProject>false</IsTestProject>
    <IsTestingPlatformApplication>false</IsTestingPlatformApplication>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <RootNamespace>AnyUnit.TestingPlatform</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Testing.Platform" Version="2.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
